298 concentration in the fishmeal. The presence of most common limiting amino acids in the
299 concentration higher than or comparable with the commercial animal feed ingredients
300 (i.e., soybean meal and fishmeal) makes BSF prepupae, pressed cake, and meal potentially
301 an ideal protein source in animal diets.
302 4 Conclusions and future recommendations
303 Overall, BSF is capable of utilizing food wastes to support its lifecycle. BSF
304 prepupae derived oil has a good fatty acids profile, which could potentially produce a high
305 quality biodiesel. Additionally, BSF prepupae, pressed cake, and meal has feed value
306 comparable to commercial feed ingredients. In-depth study, however, is required to (i)
307 account and improve the organic waste to insect biomass conversion efficiency, (ii) trans
308 esterify the insect oil into biodiesel and characterize thus produced biodiesel for fuel
309 properties, and (iii) test nutrients digestibility and palatability of insect biomass before
310 such insect biorefinery could be successfully implemented as an efficient technology for
311 generating biofuel and animal feed with simultaneous organic waste valorization.
